# Activity: Notification Toast & In-App Activity Feed Components

## 1. Objective & Context
Build an unobtrusive in-app toast component and notification dropdown bell in the navigation bar. Maintain the neutral dark, OLED-friendly aesthetic without jarring colors or layout shift.

- **Prerequisites:** Activity 14.1 (Notification Store).
- **Target Location:** `frontend/src/components/common/NotificationToast.vue` and `frontend/src/components/common/AppNavbar.vue`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Design Specifications:**
  - Background `#121215`, border `zinc-800`, text `zinc-200`.
  - Subtle fade & slide-in micro-animation in the top-right corner.
  - Auto-dismiss after 6 seconds with progress bar or manual close button.
  - Quick action buttons (e.g. "Iniciar Foco" if routine block started).
- **Navbar Integration:**
  - Bell icon with unread badge counter in `AppNavbar.vue`.
  - Dropdown panel showing latest 5 alerts and "Marcar todas como lidas" button.

## 3. Implementation Steps
1. Create `NotificationToast.vue` with TransitionGroup.
2. Embed toast container at root in `App.vue`.
3. Add bell icon and dropdown trigger to `AppNavbar.vue`.

## 4. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] In-app toast appears smoothly upon event reception.
- [ ] Dismisses automatically or via close button.
- [ ] Matches the minimalist dark palette.
